cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "ndplex: the n-Dimensional m-Plex array, a generic Pascal's array for NumPy"
abstract: >-
  A generic Pascal's array of any dimension, as a NumPy array subclass: by
  default Pascal's rectangle, cube or hypercube, with user-defined edges,
  node-generating function and argument locations. Includes lines and
  cross-sections through the array (diag), the array as a triangle,
  tetrahedron or n-simplex (as_tri), and row-by-row lookup in the On-Line
  Encyclopedia of Integer Sequences (oeis).
authors:
  - family-names: Teske
    given-names: Ted
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
# The Zenodo concept DOI and the version DOIs are added after the first
# Zenodo-archived release (0.1.0).
repository-code: "https://github.com/tedteske/ndplex"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/ndplex/"
keywords:
  - Pascal's triangle
  - Pascal's array
  - combinatorics
  - binomial coefficients
  - multinomial coefficients
  - simplex
  - integer sequences
  - OEIS
  - NumPy
references:
